I think the way you gain intrinsics should be changed a bit. 
Currently it's a kind of boolean choice; either you gain
it, or you don't.

What I propose is that you should gain intrinsics gradually;
that is, when you (e.g.) eat a poisonous corpse, you should
increase your "poison resistance" by a certain percentage
(maybe 5%-10%). That way, the first poisonous corpse would
decrease your health by 100% of a certain value, the second
poisonous corpse would decrease it by 90% of that value
and so on. At the same time, you would take a 100%, 90%, 80%...
chance of losing strength/constitution or whatever appropriate.

Same with other intrinsics, maybe the level of the corpse
could have an influence as well (eating a poisonous dragon
corpse might gain you 50% of the intrinsic "poison res.").

You could also gain abilities from the corpses that way;
for example eating a red dragon corpse would add to your
fire resistance, and at the same time give you a 5%
ability of breathing fire at your opponents in combat...
If you eat lots of red dragons, you might even gain
the ability to breath fire in 20-25%... (there should
be an upper limit for such things).

Comments?

